    "text": "Let a tangent be drawn to the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>27</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then the&nbsp;value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> such that the sum of intercepts on axes made by this tangent is minimum is equal&nbsp;to :",
    "image": null
